      "content": "thanks. one other thing though—the distribution of these pits is really weird. instead of being spread out across a whole vessel, they're clustered in these small, erratic groups in the corners of the shards or near the base. it doesn't look like a tool mark or a kiln issue. it almost looks like the clay was being nibbled at or messed with by something small and many-handed before it was even put in the kiln. does that sound like any specific type of degradation you've seen in the literature?",
